<title>LATVIA: BALTICS-SECURITIES COMMISSIONS DISCUSS COOPERATION.</title>
<headline>BALTICS-SECURITIES COMMISSIONS DISCUSS COOPERATION.</headline>
<dateline>RIGA 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The securities committees of Latvia and Lithuania held a meeting to discuss cooperation and said an agreement could be signed in September.</p>
<p>&quot;We discussed strategic issues concerning the integration of securities markets,&quot; Latvian securities commission chairman Viktor Gustsons told a news conference late Wednesday after meeting his Lithuanian counterparts.</p>
<p>&quot;In September we could sign a co-operation agreement but we have to discuss the details. We have a common understanding about the market's development,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Vergilijus Poderys, head of the Lithuanian securities committee, said that any agreement would be a framework deal, not including details. Special regulations concerning licences would follow.</p>
<p>&quot;It gives us an opportunity to work together,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>-- Riga newsroom, +371 721 5240</p>
</text>
